{"title":"Tuesday assorted links","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/919622543/0/marginalrevolution~Tuesday-assorted-links.html","date":1748965560000,"content":"<p>1. <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.nytimes.com/2025/06/02/us/trump-tariffs-court-brief.html?smid=nytcore-ios-share&amp;referringSource=articleShare&amp;sgrp=g&amp;pvid=EE172D12-9D1D-46DA-AB35-D60628200CDE\" target=\"_blank\">The coalition against the Trump tariffs</a> (NYT).</p>\r\n<p>2. “<a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.theatlantic.com/science/archive/2025/05/adam-riess-hubble-tension/682980/\" target=\"_blank\">He believes that the Hubble tension will likely grow more pronounced and that more cosmologists will start to question the standard model.</a>”</p>\r\n<p>3. <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.nytimes.com/2025/06/02/books/alasdair-macintyre-dead.html\" target=\"_blank\">Alasdair Macintyre obituary</a> (NYT).</p>\r\n<p>4. <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://x.com/BrankoMilan/status/1929286314765009339\" target=\"_blank\">Branko okie-dokie</a>.</p>\r\n<p>5. “Conjecture: econ academia is very far from the optimal architecture for data research. The optimal architecture is much more centralized. Half the researchers work together, or in large teams, to build clean and efficient datasets. The rest work in smaller teams to analyze data”  Link <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://x.com/alz_zyd_/status/1929534920747094372\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.</p>\r\n<p>6. <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://x.com/AEAjournals/status/1929549038614917136\" target=\"_blank\">In Burkina Faso, free contraception does not lower fertility much</a>.</p>\r\n<p>7. <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.nytimes.com/2025/06/03/business/xi-zho